---
import Layout from "../../components/Layout.astro";
import ToolPage from "@bt/ui/ToolPage.astro";
import AdSlot from "@bt/ui/AdSlot.astro";
import PhotoTool from "@bt/ui/PhotoTool.tsx";
import { PRESETS_MX_ES } from "@bt/ui/photo-presets";
import t from "../../i18n/en.json";
---
<Layout
  bleed
  lang="en"
  title="Mexican ID photo online: infantil, passport, credential | Baitaan"
  description="Crop your photo to infantil size (2.5 × 3 cm), passport or credential and download a print-ready sheet. Free, and your photo is never uploaded."
>
  <ToolPage
    heading="ID photo sizes: infantil and more"
    lead="Pick a photo from your phone, fit it to the size you need, and download a 10 × 15 cm or letter-size sheet ready to print. Your photo never leaves your device."
    updated="Updated: November 2026"
    sourcesHeading="Sources"
    sources={[{ href: "https://travel.state.gov/content/travel/en/us-visas/visa-information-resources/photos.html", label: "US Department of State: visa photo requirements" }]}
  >
    <PhotoTool client:visible presets={PRESETS_MX_ES} t={t.photo} sheets={["10x15", "carta"]} />

    <Fragment slot="guide">
      <h2>Common photo sizes</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Infantil:</strong> 2.5 × 3 cm. Schools, ID cards and paperwork.</li>
        <li><strong>Passport size:</strong> 3.5 × 4.5 cm. Visas and documents in many countries.</li>
        <li><strong>Credential:</strong> 3.5 × 5 cm.</li>
        <li><strong>Diploma or professional licence:</strong> 6 × 9 cm.</li>
        <li><strong>Spanish DNI and passport:</strong> 2.6 × 3.2 cm.</li>
        <li><strong>US visa:</strong> 5 × 5 cm (2 × 2 inches).</li>
      </ul>
      <p>You don't need to bring a photo for a Mexican passport: the Foreign Ministry (SRE) takes it at the office.</p>

      <h2>How to print your photos</h2>
      <ol class="ms-5 list-decimal space-y-1">
        <li>Choose the 10 × 15 cm print sheet for a photo shop, or Letter for your own printer.</li>
        <li>When printing, choose actual size or 100%. Don't use “fit to page”, which changes the size.</li>
        <li>Cut along the grey lines.</li>
      </ol>

      <AdSlot unit="0000000000" label="Advertisement" />

      <h2>Tips for an accepted photo</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>White or light background, no shadows.</li>
        <li>Facing the camera, face uncovered, neutral expression.</li>
        <li>No sunglasses or cap.</li>
        <li>Good light from the front: next to a window works well.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Each institution may ask for something different (white or coloured background, glasses or not). Check their requirements before printing.</p>

      <h2>How many photos fit on each sheet</h2>
      <p>Pixels are for printing at 300 dpi. The last two columns show how many photos the tool fits on each sheet.</p>
      <div class="overflow-x-auto">
        <table class="w-full text-sm">
          <thead><tr class="text-muted"><th class="py-2 text-start font-medium">Size</th><th class="py-2 text-end font-medium">Pixels</th><th class="py-2 text-end font-medium">10 × 15 cm sheet</th><th class="py-2 text-end font-medium">Letter sheet</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr class="border-t border-hair"><td class="py-2 ">Infantil 2.5 × 3 cm</td><td class="py-2 text-end tabular-nums">295 × 354</td><td class="py-2 text-end tabular-nums">12</td><td class="py-2 text-end tabular-nums">56</td></tr>
            <tr class="border-t border-hair"><td class="py-2 ">Passport 3.5 × 4.5 cm</td><td class="py-2 text-end tabular-nums">413 × 531</td><td class="py-2 text-end tabular-nums">6</td><td class="py-2 text-end tabular-nums">28</td></tr>
            <tr class="border-t border-hair"><td class="py-2 ">Credencial 3.5 × 5 cm</td><td class="py-2 text-end tabular-nums">413 × 591</td><td class="py-2 text-end tabular-nums">4</td><td class="py-2 text-end tabular-nums">25</td></tr>
            <tr class="border-t border-hair"><td class="py-2 ">Título 6 × 9 cm</td><td class="py-2 text-end tabular-nums">709 × 1063</td><td class="py-2 text-end tabular-nums">2</td><td class="py-2 text-end tabular-nums">8</td></tr>
            <tr class="border-t border-hair"><td class="py-2 ">US visa 5 × 5 cm</td><td class="py-2 text-end tabular-nums">600 × 600</td><td class="py-2 text-end tabular-nums">2</td><td class="py-2 text-end tabular-nums">15</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <h2>Which size for which paperwork?</h2>
      <ul class="ms-5 list-disc space-y-1">
        <li><strong>Infantil:</strong> school enrolment, school and work ID cards, job applications and most paper forms.</li>
        <li><strong>Credencial:</strong> some club, gym and company cards. If no size is given, it is almost always infantil.</li>
        <li><strong>Título:</strong> printed diplomas from some schools and universities; several ask for an oval photo and formal clothes, so check with yours.</li>
        <li><strong>Passports and visas:</strong> the Mexican passport doesn't use a printed photo, but many other countries' visas ask for 3.5 × 4.5 cm.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>The INE voter card and the Mexican passport don't need a photo either: it is taken at the office.</p>
      <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
      <details class="bt-faq"><summary>What if my photo is rejected?</summary><p>The usual reasons are a shadowed or coloured background, a tilted face, glasses reflecting light and printing with “fit to page”, which changes the size. Retake the photo by a window and print at 100%.</p></details>
      <details class="bt-faq"><summary>Print at home or at a shop?</summary><p>At a photo shop the 10 × 15 cm sheet is cheap and on photo paper. At home, use photo paper and the letter sheet.</p></details>
      <details class="bt-faq"><summary>Is my photo uploaded anywhere?</summary><p>No. Cropping and the sheet are done in your browser and the photo never leaves your device.</p></details>
    </Fragment>
  </ToolPage>
</Layout>
